        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Revealing nature — Darwin and The Origin of Species (annotated page)</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = {\n  tex: { inlineMath: [['$','$']], displayMath: [['$$','$$']] }\n};\n</script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    color: #1a1a1a;\n  }\n  .page {\n    position: relative;\n    width: 544px;\n    min-height: 761px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n  /* faint photographic background of the printed page */\n  .bg-photo {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 0;\n    width: 544px;\n    height: 761px;\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg,#f2f0ea 0%,#efeee8 55%,#dfe3d4 78%,#c8d2b8 100%);\n    z-index: 0;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    border: 1px dashed #999;\n    color: #555;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.25);\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- top-right vocabulary box ---------- */\n  .note-top {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 288px;\n    top: 6px;\n    width: 250px;\n    background: #d9b8e8;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    padding: 4px 5px;\n    z-index: 3;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- two text columns ---------- */\n  .columns {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 100px;\n    width: 544px;\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 22px;\n    z-index: 2;\n  }\n  .col {\n    width: 232px;\n    font-size: 8.6px;\n    line-height: 1.62;\n  }\n  .col.left { margin-left: 58px; }\n  .para {\n    display: flex;\n    gap: 6px;\n    margin-bottom: 9px;\n  }\n  .num {\n    width: 8px;\n    flex: 0 0 8px;\n    text-align: left;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 8px;\n  }\n  .txt { flex: 1; }\n  .noindent { padding-left: 14px; }\n  em { font-style: italic; }\n  .hl { background: #d9b8e8; }\n  .box-word {\n    background: #d9b8e8;\n    border: 1px solid #7a4b9a;\n    padding: 0 1px;\n  }\n  .ul-word { border-bottom: 1px solid #7a4b9a; }\n  .handwrite {\n    color: #c0392b;\n    font-family: \"Comic Sans MS\", cursive;\n    font-size: 7px;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- annotation boxes ---------- */\n  .note {\n    position: absolute;\n    background: #d9b8e8;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    padding: 4px 5px;\n    z-index: 3;\n  }\n  .note-adapt {\n    left: 6px;\n    top: 418px;\n    width: 258px;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n  }\n  .note-available {\n    left: 4px;\n    top: 538px;\n    width: 262px;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n  }\n  .note-variety {\n    left: 288px;\n    top: 418px;\n    width: 250px;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n  }\n  .warn { color: #d35400; }\n\n  /* ---------- footer ---------- */\n  .footer {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 22px;\n    bottom: 22px;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    z-index: 4;\n  }\n  .footer .pg {\n    display: inline-block;\n    margin-left: 26px;\n    font-size: 11px;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n  <div class=\"bg-photo\"></div>\n\n  <!-- top-right handwritten/typed vocabulary note -->\n  <div class=\"note-top\">\n    suspect v. 怀疑 n. 被怀疑者；嫌疑犯<br>\n    suspect sb.of (doing) sth.怀疑某人 (干)某事<br>\n    suspect sb.to be... 猜想某人……<br>\n    It was suspected that... 人们怀疑……\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"columns\">\n    <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->\n    <div class=\"col left\">\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\"></div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          their natural environments. After Darwin had\n          spent some time in South America, his room on\n          the ship was crowded with <span class=\"ul-word\">samples</span> of the plants\n          and animals he had collected. As he studied\n          these, he asked himself the question: how did\n          different species come to exist?\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\">3</div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          At that time, people believed that all species\n          had appeared on Earth at the same time, and\n          had not changed since. But Darwin began to\n          think differently. He noticed that some species\n          of animals were very similar to each other.\n          Maybe animals <span class=\"hl\">evolved</span> as they <span class=\"hl\">adapted</span> to their\n          changing environments? It was just an idea, but\n          enough to inspire Darwin to look for\n          more evidence.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\">4</div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          When the <em>Beagle</em> reached the Galápagos\n          Islands in 1835, Darwin saw <span class=\"hl\">a variety of</span> new\n          species, but it was the birds that interested\n          him the most. Darwin noticed that there was\n          a difference between the <span class=\"ul-word\">finches</span> on each of\n          the islands. It seemed their <span class=\"ul-word\">beaks</span> had evolved\n          according to what food was <span class=\"hl\">available</span> on that\n          particular island.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->\n    <div class=\"col right\">\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\">5</div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          Darwin <span class=\"hl\">suspected</span> that the finches had evolved\n          from a common <span class=\"box-word\">ancestor</span>, which had arrived on\n          the islands a long time before. Over time, it had\n          slowly evolved into many new species. And that\n          was the answer to how new species of plants\n          and animals came to exist: they evolved from\n          earlier ancestors.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\">6</div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          It was a completely new idea – a theory of\n          <span class=\"box-word\">evolution</span>. Darwin explained this theory in his\n          book, <em>On the Origin of Species</em>. It was not\n          published until 1859 and immediately caused\n          a storm. Many people refused to believe that\n          living things, including humans, had evolved\n          from lower forms of life. They were shocked.\n          But Darwin's scientific studies were so\n          convincing that more and more people started\n          to believe his theory.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"para\">\n        <div class=\"num\">7</div>\n        <div class=\"txt\">\n          Today, <em>On the Origin of Species</em> is regarded as\n          one of the most important works ever written.\n          It has changed ideas about life on Earth forever.\n          And it all began with the journey on the <em>Beagle</em>.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- annotation: adapt -->\n  <div class=\"note note-adapt\">\n    adapt vt. 使适应；使适合；改编；改写<br>\n    (1)adapt oneself to sth.使自己适应……<br>\n    adapt to 适应<br>\n    be adapted for... 为……改编/写；被改编成<br>\n    be adapted from... 根据……改编<br>\n    (2)adaptable adj. 能适应的，适应性强的；可改编的<br>\n    adaption/adaptation n. 适应；改编本，改写本\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- annotation: available -->\n  <div class=\"note note-available\">\n    available adj. 可获得的；可利用的；有空的<br>\n    be available to为……可利用/得到；可利用/获得<br>\n    be available from 从……处可获得<br>\n    make sth.available for/to sb. 使某人可以享受某物<br>\n    available resources/facilities 可利用的资源/设备<br>\n    (2)availably adv. 有效地；可获得地\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- annotation: a variety of -->\n  <div class=\"note note-variety\">\n    a variety of 各种各样的<br>\n    (1)variety n. 变化；种类<br>\n    a variety of＋n.＝varieties of＋n. (可数名<br>\n    词复数或不可数名词)各种各样的<br>\n    (2)vary vi. &amp; vt.有变化；改变<br>\n    vary from...to... 由……到……不等<br>\n    vary between...and...由……到……不等<br>\n    vary with sth.随着……而变化<br>\n    (3)various adj. 各种各样的；多姿多彩的<br>\n    <span class=\"warn\">⚠</span><br>\n    (1)a variety of/varieties of 后接可数名词作<br>\n    主语时，谓语动词用复数形式；<br>\n    (2)the variety of＋复数名词，意为\"……的<br>\n    品种\"，作主语时，谓语动词用单数形式。\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"footer\">\n    Revealing nature<span class=\"pg\">51</span>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
